.TH PIANO-SENSORS-CHECK 1 "October 2026" "piano" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
piano-sensors-check \- report piano SensorProxy state after a fresh boot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B piano-sensors-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the boot identity, sensor service status, five seconds of accelerometer
monitor output, and standard SensorProxy acceleration and ambient light
properties. Rotate the upright tablet and vary illumination to verify actual
hardware and GNOME behavior separately.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the reporting commands completed. It is not a hardware acceptance
result. A nonzero status indicates a failed service or reporting command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR monitor-sensor (1),
.BR busctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
